1080:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   * @brief  Enable ExtiLine Falling Edge Trigger for Lines in range 0 to 31
1081:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   * @note The configurable wakeup lines are edge-triggered. No glitch must be
1082:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       generated on these lines. If a falling edge on a configurable interrupt
1083:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       line occurs during a write operation in the EXTI_FTSR register, the
1084:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       pending bit is not set.
1085:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       Rising and falling edge triggers can be set for
1086:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       the same interrupt line. In this case, both generate a trigger
1087:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       condition.
1088:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   * @rmtoll FTSR1        FTx           LL_EXTI_EnableFallingTrig_0_31
